# The build context for Dockerfile.full, which differs from .dockerignore in
# exactly one way: this image needs the plugin modules, and the primary one
# does not.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to `.dockerignore`,
# so the two builds get different contexts from one tree rather than the
# primary image paying for sources it never compiles.
#
# Sources only, never the built artifacts. `make plugins` and a bare `go build`
# both leave a binary beside the module they came from — around 187 MB across
# the eleven of them — and every byte would be uploaded to the daemon only to
# be ignored, on a machine where somebody has been building locally. The
# exclude-then-re-include is what keeps that precise: a plugin added tomorrow
# is picked up by the `*.go` rules with nothing to update here.
plugins/**
!plugins/*/*.go
!plugins/*/go.mod
!plugins/*/go.sum

# Working documents: never shipped, see .gitignore for why.
.local/

.git/
dist/
bin/
*.test
coverage.out
coverage.html
.DS_Store

docs/
*.md
examples/
